{"title":"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_April_2026)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, April 2026)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(after_andib2n)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (after andib2n)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cdf676c3182b84e9a863fbf223c1abe492715f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. In their decimal representations, the last three digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d655eb08535de0b94232fd4973aa70f434edbd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are equal, respectively, to the last three digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be958d0ced3fbfac442fe97c2a8a48616bc4e6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> has its least value.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f77bf5eeb89eba1db6496a3b2074b0dba819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^m\\equiv 1978^n\\pmod {1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8d03c83f70e3f03bd2ca9a3d575a5047e3fff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^m-978^n=1000k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"168\" height=\"13\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (if it is not positive just do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b247f8548ec9a44e4ab37d6db1039394cd7d0f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^n-978^m=-1000k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"182\" height=\"13\" />). Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e591a44169078eabce401b76a47ff79e3530c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^n\\mid 1000k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. So dividing through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5daa8aff48a709c22cd0332c524f57670c9b54b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^n$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62965ac39f10f23a7c12f76aa9e863e791dc9a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^{m-n}-1=\\frac{1000k}{978^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"162\" height=\"37\" />. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1765f792cde5f600ebf90e216e425e8aa9a507d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\nmid LHS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec9421ed2be50845a827c94886afcdc3b9a8b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\nmid RHS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. So since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5bd88957666052f73482bce0c7d4f0d58878f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2|| 978^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, clearly the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b7590e5dde6dd53610734b116994f9cd9f001d1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$489^n\\mid k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />). We will show later that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is minimal then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is minimal. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d34f9cc0efb71ef3757b64968395bce7bb1bea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$978^{m-3}-1\\equiv 0\\pmod {125}\\Leftrightarrow 103^{m-3}\\equiv 1\\pmod {125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"419\" height=\"19\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e951611530abf69dd5cacf34d497336265dc5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-3\\mid \\varphi(125)\\Rightarrow m-3\\mid 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"18\" />. Checking by hand we find that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f53d674af320f092cf818d3639f837c2be24b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-3=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> works (this also shows that minimality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> depends on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, as claimed above). So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28893f5dfc22e54fb7c16159f3134d6ad05b009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=103$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />. Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b217fea6b5462d5a8fb675607375c5f5b29d8317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=106$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7d023653adaf6126bd7d6e52a0e14ed70b7c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(m,n)=(103,3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"143\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>The above solution was posted and copyrighted by cobbler and Andreas.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It can be seen as a video stream at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRl4Wnd60os\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRl4Wnd60os</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_April_2026.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_April_2026)\">Remarks (added by pf02, April 2026)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, April 2026)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first solution is sloppily written, and it contains some hand-waving, but it\nis essentially correct. The video solution is good, but it would be nice to see\nit written on this web page.\n</p><p>On the discussion page mentioned below, user andib2n gives an idea\nfor a solution which unlike the first two solutions does not use\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_Totient_Theorem\" title=\"Euler&#39;s Totient Theorem\">Euler's Totient Theorem</a>. As a public service, I will paraphrase\nthe solution below.\n</p><p>And, a general comment. This problem can be solved easily on a\ncomputer by writing a very small program in some language (I wrote\none in python, less than 15 lines long). The program executes in a\nfraction of a second. Even without a computer, the problem can be\nsolved by brute force, by making a few simplifying observations\nand less than 25 multiplications of 3-digit numbers. So I judge\nthe problem mathematically uninteresting, since the challenge is\nto solve it quickly without using easily available technology or\ntechniques.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28after_andib2n.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(after_andib2n)\">Solution 3 (after andib2n)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (after andib2n)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87ee779aa70f31f3ea964e704f004ecb3563e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^n \\equiv 1978^m \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" />.\nEquivalently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875c383cd97ac91218ab7fbe47efd1c1545ca83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^m (1978^{n - m} - 1) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f82cd1f016745db720ed52fe529a1226fbadce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 = 8 \\cdot 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> it can be seen easily that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d655eb08535de0b94232fd4973aa70f434edbd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> has to be\ndivisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339b24d35f55408263cd36603d768eec4557ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1978^{n - m} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" /> has to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\nThe smallest vale for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b00129906b721ebe808a705e83d5df749a4ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 3$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. We will prove that the smallest\nvalue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a585892d0b91fdff607ad453c81b972bf5af61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"22\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200cbb3a9b14cedb386e2445dc580af6dfc67c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Step 1: Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17009b666e78604a7a2a97373c66d1984ef6cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"22\" />. When we raise a\nnumber ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at successive powers, the last digit will be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1005a633a66db067904f8aa7891007fc20b7b4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8, 4, 2, 6, 8, 4, 2, 6, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />. Clearly, in order to have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17009b666e78604a7a2a97373c66d1984ef6cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"22\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nLet us say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5de80d19ed368b3c05c278433c9fcb1ae1bfb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Step 2. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8c4b794b90fb26e13e780a32dc174d6b4b0d42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^{4p} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"21\" />. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c905cbfa39898302ab0f006a0329f2e9bbbc86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^4 \\equiv 3^4 = 81 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"243\" height=\"21\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16226319a658d9dcdd6828c7e8326614e6c43d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^{4p} \\equiv (5 + 1)^p \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"21\" />. Thinking of the binomial\nexpansion, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b836f0bca3d50395a603c1859f56276f06d24e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5 + 1)^p = M \\cdot 5^2 + p \\cdot 5 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" /> for\nsome <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. For this to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/0437b82b945f1f6e8d2d41d8752c052db73242e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 1 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" /> we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be a\nmultiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let us say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac9eee81c36e414b2cf177cf356ed362dce3c409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 5q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a9492248b4cf8eba267b95f038223bab31f830ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 20q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Step 3. Find the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abee1b1c167daee6f950c5f40eee4d049f09c049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^{20q} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"21\" />.\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f577fc386309c2fc525c1f1092cbd68d8fa1f6f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^{20} \\equiv 3^{20} = 81^5 \\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"240\" height=\"21\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ee9b4a88a8bd91049ea547fb1ab4936dfbb1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1978^{20q} \\equiv (80 + 1)^{5q} \\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"21\" />. Thinking of the binomial\nexpansion, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1fcbc54bec96feb7018f11fa5f83f478125bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(80 + 1)^{5q} = M \\cdot 80^3 + \\frac{5q(5q - 1)}{2} \\cdot 80^2 + 5q \\cdot 80 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"411\" height=\"40\" />\nfor some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. The first term is obviously divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> (because\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba43df64b5cc2d125c8b113817f5d28671ee3056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80 = 5 \\cdot 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />), and the second term is also divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. For\nthe third term to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be divisible by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The smallest value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd4080d7328aa3d96b48312d992f1d2f9f1a38c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200cbb3a9b14cedb386e2445dc580af6dfc67c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that the smallest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561547b977c3c43aa98fde43cb8d7f7907c4dcff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - m$\" width=\"48\" height=\"8\" /> is 100, so the smallest\nvalue for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/276654f5f58da634d19f21bafacb851e246026df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 103$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/c6h61017\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO\" title=\"1978 IMO\">1978 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> 